# Crew beats: small human moments, most of the log. Idle-friendly beats make an
# absent player's astronaut look good. House style: content/STYLE.md.

card beat_coffee
type beat
days 3 42
weight 8
once
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} and {B} rebuild the coffee maker's heater. It now settles in forty seconds. {B} wants it faster. {A} is worried about overshoot. The coffee is excellent either way.
do bond A B 5

card beat_cards
type beat
days 2 42
weight 8
cooldown 12
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} teaches {B} a card game from home. By the end of the shift {B} is winning, and the rules have been amended twice.
do bond A B 5

card beat_window
type beat
days 1 8
weight 12
once
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} and {B} take turns at the window as Earth and the Moon slide into the same frame. Neither says anything for a long time. Neither needs to.
do bond A B 6

card beat_gym
type beat
days 3 42
weight 7
cooldown 9
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} and {B} share the exercise slot, two hours a day so their bones still work at Mars. They keep score. Nobody knows what the score measures.
do bond A B 4
do morale A 2

card beat_zipties
type beat
days 10 42
weight 6
once
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} and {B} finally agree on which drawer the zip ties live in. It has taken the whole flight so far, and it may be the most important engineering decision made aboard.
do bond A B 4

card beat_haircut
type beat
days 12 42
weight 5
once
roles A B
when same A B
when bond A B >= 0
text {A} cuts {B}'s hair with the vacuum clippers. The result is logged as "within tolerance". {B} agrees and tips in coffee.
do bond A B 5

card beat_home_msg
type beat
days 8 42
weight 6
cooldown 10
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} records a message for a school group back home that's been following the fleet. The kids send back forty questions, mostly about the toilet. {A} answers every one.
do morale A 4
do trait A warm 2

card beat_shelter_night
type beat
days 6 42
weight 5
cooldown 12
roles A B
when same A B
when var storms >= 1
text {A} and {B} reorganize the storm shelter between the water tanks so the next flare night is less miserable. Two more sleeping spots, one hook for the cards, and a sign that reads "the Sun is not your friend".
do bond A B 4

card beat_early_watch
type beat
days 1 8
weight 10
cooldown 3
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} and {B} stand the night watch. Earth still fills most of the window, blue and close. They talk about home as if it were down the road. Each day it's a little less true.
do bond A B 5

# --- Idle-friendly: only for astronauts whose owner hasn't been in for a while ----
card idle_watch
type beat
days 4 42
weight 10
cooldown 10
roles A
when idle A >= 3
when cond A ok
text {A} takes an extra night watch so everyone else can sleep before the burn. Nobody asked. The log entry is two lines long and perfectly neat.
do morale A 2
do trait A warm 2

card idle_mentor
type beat
days 6 42
weight 8
cooldown 12
roles A B
when idle A >= 3
when same A B
when cond B ok
text {A} walks {B} through the backup docking procedure step by step, until {B} can do it without the checklist. Neither of them mentions why it matters.
do bond B A 6
do trait B brave 2

card idle_spares
type beat
days 8 42
weight 8
cooldown 9
roles A
when idle A >= 4
when cond A ok
text {A} inventories the spares locker by hand and finds a filter cartridge the manifest says was never loaded. Somebody at Starbase packed a margin. {A} logs it and says a quiet thank-you to whoever it was.
do res spares 1
